        "tool_call_id": "call_SFyBKZwhw9worXRwyd0Qr8nR",
        "content": "=== attack ===\n  desc: Melee attack an adjacent monster in the given direction. Do NOT call if the target shows `[PET — don't attack]` in ADJACENT — attacking a pet damages alignment. Walk around pets instead.\n  schema: {'properties': {'direction': {'title': 'Direction', 'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['direction'], 'title': 'attackArguments', 'type': 'object'}\n\n=== descend ===\n  desc: Descend the down-staircase. You MUST be standing on a '>' tile. Check `=== UNDER PLAYER ===` first — it should say 'stairs DOWN (>)'. If it says 'stairs UP (<)' you'll go BACK to a previous level inst\n  schema: {'properties': {}, 'title': 'descendArguments', 'type': 'object'}\n\n=== search ===\n  desc: Search adjacent tiles for hidden passages and traps. Pass `times` to repeat — hidden passages typically need 5-10 searches at the same tile to reveal. Defaults to 1.\n  schema: {'properties': {'times': {'default': 1, 'title': 'Times', 'type': 'integer'}}, 'title': 'searchArguments', 'type': 'object'}\n\n=== eat ===\n  desc: Eat an edible item from inventory. Pass `item` = substring of the food's description (e.g. 'apple', 'food ration') OR its inventory letter. If no edible items exist or `item` doesn't match, the turn i\n  schema: {'properties': {'item': {'default': None, 'title': 'Item', 'type': 'string'}}, 'title': 'eatArguments', 'type': 'object'}\n\n=== quaff ===\n  desc: Quaff (drink) a potion. Pass `item` = substring or letter. If no potion matches, the turn is NOT consumed.\n  schema: {'properties': {'item': {'default': None, 'title': 'Item', 'type': 'string'}}, 'title': 'quaffArguments', 'type': 'object'}\n\n=== read ===\n  desc: Read a scroll or spellbook. Pass `item` = substring or letter. If no readable matches, the turn is NOT consumed.\n  schema: {'properties': {'item': {'default': None, 'title': 'Item', 'type': 'string'}}, 'title': 'readArguments', 'type': 'object'}\n\n=== pray ===\n  desc: Pray to your god (#pray, then 'y' to confirm). Risky if recently used.\n  schema: {'properties': {}, 'title': 'prayArguments', 'type': 'object'}\n\n=== engrave_elbereth ===\n  desc: Engrave 'Elbereth' in the dust to scare most monsters. Uses E command.\n  schema: {'properties': {}, 'title': 'engrave_elberethArguments', 'type': 'object'}\n\n=== kick ===\n  desc: Kick (ctrl-D) in a direction. Used to break locks/doors. Pass `direction` (N/NE/.../NW).\n  schema: {'properties': {'direction': {'default': 'N', 'title': 'Direction', 'type': 'string'}}, 'title': 'kickArguments', 'type': 'object'}\n\n=== throw ===\n  desc: Throw an item in a direction. Pass `item` (substring/letter) AND `direction`.\n  schema: {'properties': {'item': {'title': 'Item', 'type': 'string'}, 'direction': {'default': 'N', 'title': 'Direction', 'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['item'], 'title': 'throwArguments', 'type': 'object'}\n\n=== pickup ===\n  desc: Pick up items on the current tile.\n  schema: {'properties': {}, 'title': 'pickupArguments', 'type': 'object'}\n\n=== move_to ===\n  desc: Pathfind to a specific (x, y) tile on the current level. Uses A* over the visible map. The path is precomputed — if a monster steps into the path mid-traversal, the rollout will end up engaging it. Fo\n  schema: {'properties': {'x': {'title': 'X', 'type': 'integer'}, 'y': {'title': 'Y', 'type': 'integer'}}, 'required': ['x', 'y'], 'title': 'move_toArguments', 'type': 'object'}\n\n=== explore_and_descend ===\n  desc: CLOSED-LOOP mega-skill: automatically explore the ENTIRE current level (revealing rooms/corridors, and SEARCHING dead-ends and door-adjacent walls for hidden passages), and the instant the down-stairc\n  schema: {'properties': {'max_floors': {'default': 1, 'title': 'Max Floors', 'type': 'integer'}, 'max_game_steps': {'default': 120, 'title': 'Max Game Steps', 'type': 'integer'}, 'max_seconds': {'default': 60.0, 'title': 'Max Seconds', 'type': 'number'}}, 'title': 'explore_and_descendArguments', 'type': 'object'}\n\n=== add_note ===\n  desc: Write or overwrite a note under a keyed slot. Use this to remember facts that will be useful many turns later: item locations, monster behaviors, dungeon layout summaries. Keep notes terse and concret\n  schema: {'properties': {'key': {'title': 'Key', 'type': 'string'}, 'text': {'title': 'Text', 'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['key', 'text'], 'title': 'add_noteArguments', 'type': 'object'}\n\n=== recall ===\n  desc: Search your notes for the given query substring. Returns matching (key, text) pairs. Use this when you suspect you've seen something before but can't remember the detail.\n  schema: {'properties': {'query': {'title': 'Query', 'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['query'], 'title': 'recallArguments', 'type': 'object'}\n\n=== pin_objective ===\n  desc: Set your current top-level objective. Always rendered into every observation thereafter. Replace as your strategy evolves.\n  schema: {'properties': {'text': {'title': 'Text', 'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['text'], 'title': 'pin_objectiveArguments', 'type': 'object'}\n\n=== wiki_lookup ===\n  desc: Fetch a named NetHack wiki page (e.g. 'cockatrice', 'mine town'). Use when you've identified a specific monster or feature and want the canonical lore.\n  schema: {'properties': {'entity': {'title': 'Entity', 'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['entity'], 'title': 'wiki_lookupArguments', 'type': 'object'}\n\n=== wiki_search ===\n  desc: Substring-search the NetHack wiki. Returns up to k pages whose title or body contain the query. Use for fuzzy / exploratory questions ('what beats stunning?').\n  schema: {'properties': {'query': {'title': 'Query', 'type': 'string'}, 'k': {'default': 3, 'title': 'K', 'type': 'integer'}}, 'required': ['query'], 'title': 'wiki_searchArguments', 'type': 'object'}\n\n",
